      "text": "To determine how far the tip of the second hand travels in 30 minutes, we need to calculate the distance it covers in one minute and then multiply by 30.\n\nFirst, let's find the circumference of the circle traced by the second hand. The second hand completes one full circle every minute, so the circumference \\( C \\) of the circle is given by:\n\\[\nC = 2 \\pi r\n\\]\nwhere \\( r \\) is the length of the second hand. Here, the length \\( r \\) is 6 cm, so:\n\\[\nC = 2 \\pi \\times 6 = 12 \\pi \\text{ cm}\n\\]\n\nNext, we need to determine how far the tip of the second hand travels in 30 minutes. Since the second hand completes one full circle every minute, in 30 minutes it will complete 30 full circles. Therefore, the total distance \\( D \\) traveled by the tip of the second hand in 30 minutes is:\n\\[\nD = 30 \\times 12 \\pi = 360 \\pi \\text{ cm}\n\\]\n\nThus, the distance traveled by the tip of the second hand during a period of 30 minutes is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{360\\pi}\n\\]",
