      "text": "To determine the distance traveled by the tip of the second hand in 30 minutes, we need to consider the path it traces out. The second hand moves in a circular path around the center of the clock, and we can use the formula for the circumference of a circle to find the distance traveled.\n\nThe formula for the circumference \\( C \\) of a circle with radius \\( r \\) is:\n\\[ C = 2 \\pi r \\]\n\nHere, the radius \\( r \\) of the circle traced by the tip of the second hand is 6 cm. So, the circumference of the circle is:\n\\[ C = 2 \\pi \\times 6 = 12 \\pi \\text{ cm} \\]\n\nSince the second hand completes one full circle every 60 minutes, in 30 minutes it will complete half of a full circle. Therefore, the distance traveled by the tip of the second hand in 30 minutes is half of the circumference:\n\\[ \\text{Distance} = \\frac{12 \\pi}{2} = 6 \\pi \\text{ cm} \\]\n\nThus, the distance traveled by the tip of the second hand during a period of 30 minutes is:\n\\[ \\boxed{6\\pi} \\]",
